WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.500
Planning connects the observation objective to a safe and lawful method.

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:08.900
Review the location, applicable rules, airspace, property access, terrain, obstacles, people,

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:13.700
nearby operations, and current official restrictions before selecting a route or platform.

00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:17.700
Weather and lighting affect both aircraft safety and evidence quality.

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:20.500
Wind, visibility, precipitation, temperature, glare, cloud cover,

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:23.300
and shadows may change during the mission.

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:27.300
Select conditions that fit equipment limitations and the analytical question.

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:31.700
Identify a controlled launch and recovery area when using a drone.

00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:35.700
Plan battery margins for takeoff, collection, return, contingencies, and landing.

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:41.700
Do not build a route that depends on ideal endurance or an uninterrupted communication link.

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:46.500
Design a flight path or observation sequence that covers the authorized area

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:48.900
with the required angle and overlap.

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:52.500
Keep unnecessary private areas outside the frame where practical.

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:56.100
Mark decision points for returning, landing, or ending collection.

00:00:56.100 --> 00:01:00.100
Prepare emergency options for changing weather, low battery, signal loss,

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:04.500
people entering the area, navigation problems, or an unavailable recovery point.

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:08.500
Brief crew communication and define who can call a stop.

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:12.100
Document objective, location, crew, platform, permissions, official-source checks, weather,

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:15.700
lighting, hazards, controls, route, collection settings, and emergency actions.

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:20.100
A written plan supports repeatability and later interpretation of the imagery.

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:24.100
Review the plan immediately before collection because conditions can change.

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:29.300
A route that was reasonable during desktop planning may become unsuitable when people,

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:32.100
vehicles, glare, wind, or temporary activity appear.
